course: dictionary
lesson: 13026
title: Factual words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Factual means based on facts: things that are true and real, not made up. A factual book about sharks tells you real things about sharks, such as how many teeth they have. «The report gave facts about the rainforest, including how much rain falls there each year.» Every fact in that report can be checked.
explain: Fiction is different. A story can be wonderful, but its characters and events are invented. «The dragon flew over the castle and breathed fire.» Dragons are not real, so this is fiction, not factual writing.
explain: To test a sentence, ask: can this be checked and shown to be true? «Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius.» That can be checked, so it is factual. «Water is the most beautiful thing in the world.» That is an opinion, so it is not factual.
fact: Factual means based on facts: true and real, not made up.
fact: «Factual» can also mean giving facts and information, not stories or opinions.
fact: A «factual error» is a mistake in the facts, such as saying a whale is a fish.
fact: Non-fiction books are factual, and so are reports, instructions and explanations.
fact: In an exam, «give a factual account» means simply tell what happened, without adding your own opinion.
exercise: «The report told us that penguins cannot fly.» Is this sentence factual? | No, it is a made-up story | *Yes, it can be checked and it is true | No, it is only an opinion
exercise: Which is a factual book? | A poem about the moon | *A non-fiction book about volcanoes | A fairy tale about a talking volcano
exercise: Which sentence is an opinion, not a fact? | *Dogs are the best pets in the whole world | Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius | Dogs are mammals
test: «The factual report used numbers and maps.» What does factual mean here? | Sung like a song | Written in rhyme | *Based on facts, true and real | Made up for a funny story
test: What is a mistake in the facts called? | Rhyme | Fiction | *A factual error | Opinion
exam: Jade says her story about a talking dragon is factual. Who is right? | Jade, because she wrote it herself | Nobody, because facts cannot be checked | Jade, because all stories are factual | *Her teacher, because a talking dragon is made up, so it is fiction
